<p>Thanks!</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I don't think it's as horrifying as other co76 entries but it's got a unique flair</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Co76 horror has always been something I've found really interesting, yet really hard to replicate. It tends to walk a fine line between horror and pathos, generally straying into more the realm of horror by leaving more things unexplained. But here I guess we opted for a more comprehensible story, and that's why it feels a little different from other Co76 works. At least that's my guess.</p>

